# SEO and static build

Every routed page must set metadata and structured data in its constructor.

```typescript
constructor() {
  const seo = inject(SeoService);
  const jsonLd = inject(JsonLdService);
  seo.set({ title: 'Projects', description: '…', path: '/projects' });
  jsonLd.upsert('person', jsonLd.person());
  jsonLd.upsert('breadcrumb', jsonLd.breadcrumb([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Projects', path: '/projects' },
  ]));
}
```

- `path` is site-root-relative (`/`, `/knowledge/slug`). `SeoService` derives the absolute base from `siteUrl` or `document.baseURI`.
- Prefer `JsonLdService` helpers (`person`, `website`, `article`, `faqPage`, `breadcrumb`) over one-off hardcoded origins.
- New public routes: add `app.routes.ts`, `scripts/build-meta.mjs` `STATIC_ROUTES`, and the postbuild route list so GitHub Pages deep links get a folder shell.

## Scripts

- `npm run content` / `prebuild` → `scripts/build-meta.mjs` (articles, sitemap, `llms.txt`).
- `postbuild` / `build:pages` → `scripts/postbuild.mjs` (per-route `index.html`, `.nojekyll`).
- GitHub Pages: `npm run build:pages` uses `--base-href=/PersonalPortfolio/`.
